<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton of Bern</h1><p class="st-meta">1218 CE – 1798 CE · capital Bern</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aristocratic city-republic that grew into the largest state of the Swiss Confederacy, ruling from the Aare to Lake Geneva until 1798.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berthold-v-duke-of-zahringen">Berthold V of Zähringen</a> founded Bern on a loop of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a> in 1191. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-zahringen">Zähringen</a> line died out in 1218 the town became an imperial city. It expanded by buying and conquering lands, defeated a coalition of nobles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-laupen">Laupen</a> in 1339, and joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Old Swiss Confederacy</a> in 1353.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A narrow circle of patrician families ruled through the Great and Small Councils. Bern conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1415 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaud">Vaud</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Savoy</a> in 1536, creating the largest city-state north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. It led the Swiss against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adrian-von-bubenberg">Adrian von Bubenberg</a> holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-morat">Murten</a> in 1476. Bern adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1528, and its finances drew on farming and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>French troops defeated Bern at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grauholz">Grauholz</a> in 1798, and it was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>, losing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaud">Vaud</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a>. It re-emerged as a canton in 1803 and became the federal city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Switzerland</a> in 1848.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/canton-of-bern.jpg" alt="Canton of Bern" width="320" height="144"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_Kanton_Bern_Canton_de_Berne.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1218 CE – 1798 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bern</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adrian von Bubenberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Reformed Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alemannic German, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Bern, Bern</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1508&amp;focus=canton-of-bern" aria-label="Canton of Bern on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4855 529 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton of Bern lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5175 785L5229 694M5175 785L5186 782M5175 785L5188 772M5175 785L5156 798M5175 785L5192 769"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5186 782h0M5188 772h0M5156 798h0M5192 769h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5175 785h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5175 785h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bern. <a href="/atlas?year=1508&amp;focus=canton-of-bern">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
